{
  "_comment": "Investigation trace card naming cases. Each is a stored final answer (`answer`) and the names the graph gives its ids (`names`). The trace route returns the answer as stored plus `final_answer_names`, the names of the ids in it (tests/unit/test_investigation_trace_card_names.py); the card applies them after the markdown is parsed (frontend/src/test/investigation-trace-names.test.tsx). The card must render the named answer with exactly the elements of the stored answer, show every `shown` string as text and no `absent` string. `chat_trace`, on single-paragraph prose answers, is both what the chat trace's `id_name_resolver.annotate_ids_in_text` makes of the answer and the text the card shows, so the two views name ids one way. Ids and names are made up.",
